{# One card per lot: the auction sheet on the left, everything read off it on
   the right. Self-contained by construction — the only <img> is a data URI and
   the only external URLs are hyperlinks back to banzai24, which the page never
   needs to load.

   Cards are grouped by whether the sheet says this is the car the search asked
   for. Requirement verdicts print **against the value they judge** rather than
   in a block of their own — the same convention the cross-checks follow, and
   for the same reason: a verdict qualifies a number best when it is printed on
   it. The only summary is the group heading, plus one line on cards that are
   not in the top group. #}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>{{ run_name }} · auction review</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --ink: #1a1a1a; --muted: #6b6b6b; --line: #e0ddd7; --paper: #faf9f7;
    --card: #ffffff; --bad: #b3261e; --ok: #1f7a4d; --warn: #9a6700;
    --money: #1a4f8a; --flat: #6b6b6b;
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body {
    margin: 0; padding: 2rem 1.5rem 4rem; background: var(--paper); color: var(--ink);
    font: 15px/1.5 -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", "Helvetica Neue",
          "Hiragino Sans", "Yu Gothic", Meiryo, sans-serif;
  }
  .wrap { max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; }

  header h1 { margin: 0 0 .25rem; font-size: 1.4rem; font-weight: 600; }
  header .meta { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: .875rem; }
  header .notes { margin: .75rem 0 0; padding: 0; list-style: none;
                  color: var(--warn); font-size: .8125rem; }

  /* The group heading is the page's spine, so it gets more weight than any
     badge on a card — the first question is which pile a car is in. */
  .group { margin: 2.5rem 0 0; padding-bottom: .3rem; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--line);
           font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: .01em; }
  .group .n { color: var(--muted); font-weight: 400; }
  .group.meets { border-bottom-color: var(--ok); }
  .group.unconfirmed { border-bottom-color: var(--flat); }
  .group.fails { border-bottom-color: var(--bad); }
  .group + .blurb { margin: .25rem 0 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: .8125rem; }

  .lot {
    background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px;
    margin: 1.25rem 0; overflow: hidden;
  }
  .lot.flagged { border-left: 4px solid var(--warn); }
  .lot.mismatch { border-left-color: var(--bad); }

  .head {
    display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .5rem 1rem; align-items: baseline;
    padding: .75rem 1rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); background: #fcfbfa;
  }
  .head .lotno { font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .head .where { color: var(--muted); font-size: .875rem; }
  .head .status { margin-left: auto; color: var(--muted); font-size: .75rem;
                  letter-spacing: .04em; text-transform: uppercase; }

  .badges { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .35rem; }
  .badge {
    font-size: .6875rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: .02em;
    padding: .15rem .45rem; border-radius: 4px; color: #fff; background: var(--flat);
    text-transform: uppercase; white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .badge.mismatch { background: var(--bad); }
  .badge.low-confidence { background: var(--warn); }

  /* Why this card is not in the top group, said once, above the fields. */
  .verdict { margin: 0; padding: .5rem 1rem; font-size: .8125rem;
             border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); background: #fdf8f7; color: var(--bad); }
  .verdict.unconfirmed { background: #f8f8f7; color: var(--muted); }

  .body { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1.25rem; padding: 1rem; align-items: flex-start; }
  /* Sheet and photo strip share a column so the strip sits *under* the sheet
     rather than beside it — in a bare flex row it would become a third column.
     The width lives on the column rather than on the sheet image, because the
     strip has to be told how wide "one line" is: shots that size themselves
     from their own pixels would push the column out to a row of full-size
     photographs and shove the fields off the card. */
  .left { flex: 0 0 auto; width: 320px; max-width: 100%; }
  .sheet { display: block; }
  .sheet img {
    /* `height: auto` is load-bearing: the img carries width/height attributes so
       the page reserves the right box before the (large, inline) data URI
       decodes, and without this the 800px height attribute wins over the CSS
       width and every sheet renders stretched to a tall ribbon. */
    display: block; width: 100%; height: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 4px; cursor: zoom-in; background: #fff;
  }
  /* CSS-only zoom: no JavaScript, so the page is inert wherever it is opened. */
  .zoom { position: absolute; opacity: 0; pointer-events: none; }
  /* Zooming widens the column, so the strip under the sheet grows with it. */
  .left:has(.sheet-zoom:checked) { width: 800px; }
  .sheet-zoom:checked + .sheet img { cursor: zoom-out; }
  /* An 800px sheet leaves the fields column a squeezed strip beside it, so the
     zoomed state drops the fields onto their own full-width row instead. The
     checkbox now sits inside .left, so this asks the row rather than reaching
     across siblings — the photo checkboxes live in there too, and they must not
     answer it, hence the class rather than a bare :has(:checked). */
  .body:has(.sheet-zoom:checked) .fields { flex: 1 1 100%; }
  /* One row, always: the shots divide whatever width the sheet column has, so
     the strip cannot wrap to a second line however many came down. Four is what
     fetch downloads; the rest are on the lot page this card links to. */
  .photos { display: flex; gap: .3rem; margin-top: .3rem; }
  .shot { flex: 1 1 0; min-width: 0; aspect-ratio: 4 / 3; display: block; }
  .shot img {
    width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; display: block;
    border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 4px; background: #fff;
    cursor: zoom-in;
  }
  /* Full size means full size: the checked shot's *label* becomes the overlay,
     covering the viewport and centring the photograph inside it. The label is
     what the click toggles, so the whole darkened field dismisses it — and the
     backdrop is a background colour rather than an element, which keeps this a
     strip of images and not a widget with a lightbox in it. */
  .photo-zoom:checked + .shot {
    position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: 20; aspect-ratio: auto;
    display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    padding: 1.5rem; background: rgba(0, 0, 0, .72); cursor: zoom-out;
  }
  .photo-zoom:checked + .shot img {
    width: auto; height: auto; max-width: 100%; max-height: 100%;
    object-fit: contain; cursor: zoom-out;
  }
  .photo-zoom:focus-visible + .shot img { outline: 2px solid var(--money); outline-offset: 2px; }

  .sheet .nosheet {
    width: 100%; height: 240px; display: flex; align-items: center;
    justify-content: center; border: 1px dashed var(--line); border-radius: 4px;
    color: var(--muted); font-size: .875rem; text-align: center; padding: 1rem;
  }

  .fields { flex: 1 1 20rem; min-width: 0; }
  .fields h2 { margin: 0 0 .5rem; font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .fields h2 .year { color: var(--muted); font-weight: 400; }
  dl { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 8.5rem 1fr; gap: .3rem .75rem; margin: 0; }
  dt { color: var(--muted); font-size: .8125rem; }
  dd { margin: 0; min-width: 0; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  dd.ja { font-size: .9375rem; white-space: pre-wrap; }

  .ok::after   { content: " ✓"; color: var(--ok); }
  .bad::after  { content: " ✗"; color: var(--bad); font-weight: 700; }
  /* Requirement verdicts carry their own classes rather than reusing the
     cross-check ones: a cross-check with nothing to compare prints no marker,
     while a requirement with nothing to answer it prints "?" — that is the
     whole difference between the two, and it is worth seeing. */
  .req-pass::after    { content: " ✓"; color: var(--ok); }
  .req-fail::after    { content: " ✗"; color: var(--bad); font-weight: 700; }
  .req-unknown::after { content: " ?"; color: var(--muted); }
  .note { color: var(--muted); font-size: .8125rem; }
  .bad + .note, .note.bad, .req-fail + .note { color: var(--bad); }
  /* The English rendering sits under the Japanese it translates, never beside
     it — the two run together otherwise, and the ja text is pre-wrapped. */
  .note.translation { display: block; margin-top: .25rem; }
  code { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; font-size: .9375rem; }

  .marks { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .3rem; }
  .mark {
    border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 4px; padding: .1rem .4rem;
    font-size: .8125rem; background: #fbfaf8;
  }
  .mark b { font-family: ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace; }
  /* The mark that disqualified the car, rather than a list you re-scan yourself. */
  .mark.banned { border-color: var(--bad); background: #fdf3f2; color: var(--bad); }

  /* The three parts of the bid arithmetic stack rather than run together on one
     line: the last of them is the number you type into the bidding platform, and
     it has to be findable at a glance rather than read out of a sentence. */
  .money span { display: block; }
  .money .result { color: var(--money); font-weight: 600; }
  .money .why { color: var(--muted); font-size: .8125rem; font-weight: 400; }

  .warn { color: var(--warn); font-weight: 600; }
  .unset { color: var(--muted); }
  details summary { cursor: pointer; color: var(--muted); font-size: .8125rem; }
  details ul { margin: .4rem 0 0; padding-left: 1.1rem; font-size: .875rem; }

  footer { margin-top: 3rem; padding-top: 1rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
           color: var(--muted); font-size: .8125rem; }
  footer dl { grid-template-columns: 2.5rem 1fr; gap: .2rem .5rem; max-width: 26rem; }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .body { flex-direction: column; }
    .left, .left:has(.sheet-zoom:checked) { width: 100%; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">

{% macro card(view) %}
{% set lot = view.lot %}
{% set top = view.flags[0].key if view.flags else '' %}
{# The zoom checkbox is keyed on the lot number rather than a loop counter:
   cards are emitted group by group, so a per-loop index would collide across
   headings and one click would zoom a different card. #}
{% set zoom_id = 'zoom-' ~ lot.lot_number %}
<article class="lot {{ 'flagged' if view.flags }} {{ top }}">

  <div class="head">
    <span class="lotno">Lot {{ lot.lot_short }}</span>
    <span class="where">
      {{ lot.auction_name }} · {{ lot.trade_date }}{% if lot.trade_time %} {{ lot.trade_time }}{% endif %}
    </span>
    <span class="badges">
      {% for flag in view.flags %}
      <span class="badge {{ flag.key }}">{{ flag.label }}</span>
      {% endfor %}
    </span>
    <span class="status">{{ lot.status_code or '—' }}</span>
  </div>

  {% if view.verdict_line %}
  <p class="verdict {{ view.group }}">{{ view.verdict_line }}</p>
  {% endif %}

  <div class="body">
    <div class="left">
      {# The checkbox precedes .sheet so `:checked +` can reach it; it is visually
         hidden but still keyboard-reachable. #}
      <input type="checkbox" class="zoom sheet-zoom" id="{{ zoom_id }}"
             aria-label="Enlarge the auction sheet for lot {{ lot.lot_short }}">
      <label class="sheet" for="{{ zoom_id }}">
        {% if view.sheet_uri %}
        <img src="{{ view.sheet_uri }}" alt="Auction sheet for lot {{ lot.lot_short }}"
             width="800" height="800">
        {% else %}
        <span class="nosheet">
          {% if lot.sheet_status == 'no_sheet' %}
          banzai24 published no sheet for this lot
          {% else %}
          sheet not downloaded ({{ lot.sheet_status }})
          {% endif %}
        </span>
        {% endif %}
      </label>

      {# The car itself, under the sheet that describes it — as many shots as
         fetch brought down, which is however many fit this one row. There is no
         "and N more" line because the number is not known here and would cost a
         column to store; the lot page in Links is the rest of the gallery. #}
      {% if view.photo_uris %}
      <div class="photos">
        {% for photo_uri in view.photo_uris %}
        <input type="checkbox" class="zoom photo-zoom" id="{{ zoom_id }}-photo-{{ loop.index }}"
               aria-label="View photo {{ loop.index }} of lot {{ lot.lot_short }} full size">
        <label class="shot" for="{{ zoom_id }}-photo-{{ loop.index }}">
          <img src="{{ photo_uri }}" loading="lazy"
               alt="Photo {{ loop.index }} of lot {{ lot.lot_short }}">
        </label>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
      {% endif %}
    </div>

    <div class="fields">
      <h2>
        {{ view.title }}
        {% if view.registration %}<span class="year">· {{ view.registration }}</span>{% endif %}
      </h2>

      <dl>
        <dt>Grade</dt>
        <dd>
          <span class="{{ view.check('grade') | verdict or (view.checks.grade | check if view.checks else '') }}">
            {{ (view.extraction.sheet_grade if view.extraction else None) or lot.grade_origin or '—' }}
          </span>
          {% if view.extraction %}
            {% if view.extraction.exterior_grade %}· exterior {{ view.extraction.exterior_grade }}{% endif %}
            {% if view.extraction.interior_grade %}· interior {{ view.extraction.interior_grade }}{% endif %}
          {% endif %}
          {% if view.check('grade') and view.check('grade').detail %}
          <span class="note bad">({{ view.check('grade').detail }})</span>
          {% elif view.grade_note %}<span class="note bad">({{ view.grade_note }})</span>{% endif %}
        </dd>

        <dt>Mileage</dt>
        <dd>
          {% if view.extraction and view.extraction.sheet_mileage_km is not none %}
          <span class="{{ view.check('mileage') | verdict or view.checks.mileage | check }}">{{ view.extraction.sheet_mileage_km | km }}</span>
          {% if view.mileage_note %}<span class="note">({{ view.mileage_note }})</span>{% endif %}
          {% else %}
          {{ lot.mileage_km | km or '—' }} <span class="note">(API, rounded)</span>
          {% endif %}
        </dd>

        {% if view.extraction %}
        <dt>Chassis</dt>
        <dd>
          <code class="{{ view.checks.chassis | check }}">{{ view.extraction.chassis_full or '—' }}</code>
          {% if view.chassis_note %}<span class="note">({{ view.chassis_note }})</span>{% endif %}
        </dd>
        {% endif %}

        {# Drivetrain shows whenever the search asks for one, extraction or not:
           its "?" is the reason a card sits in *unconfirmed*, and hiding the row
           would hide the reason. #}
        {% if view.check('drivetrain') %}
        <dt>Drivetrain</dt>
        <dd>
          <span class="{{ view.check('drivetrain') | verdict }}">
            {{ (view.extraction.drivetrain if view.extraction else None) or 'not on the sheet' }}
          </span>
          {% if view.check('drivetrain').detail and view.check('drivetrain').failed %}
          <span class="note bad">(wanted {{ view.requirements.drivetrain }})</span>
          {% endif %}
        </dd>
        {% endif %}

        {% if view.extraction %}
        <dt>Shaken 車検</dt>
        <dd>
          {% if view.extraction.shaken_expiry_raw %}
          {{ view.extraction.shaken_expiry_raw }}
          {% else %}
          <span class="warn">none — the buyer re-registers</span>
          {% endif %}
        </dd>
        {% endif %}

        {# The damage row is the assertion, not the inventory: when the search
           bans codes, the label says which and the verdict marker answers it.
           The marks themselves are still listed, with the offending one picked
           out — you still have to look at the scan, and the code tells you where. #}
        {% if view.check('damage') %}
        <dt>Damage</dt>
        <dd>
          <span class="{{ view.check('damage') | verdict }}">no {{ view.banned_codes | join('/') }} marks</span>
          {% if view.damage_marks %}
          <div class="marks">
            {% for mark in view.damage_marks %}
            <span class="mark {{ 'banned' if mark.banned }}"
                  title="{{ mark.meaning or 'not in the printed legend' }}">
              <b>{{ mark.code }}</b> {{ mark.panel }}
            </span>
            {% endfor %}
          </div>
          {% elif view.extraction %}
          <span class="note">(diagram clean)</span>
          {% endif %}
        </dd>
        {% elif view.damage_marks %}
        <dt>Damage</dt>
        <dd>
          <div class="marks">
            {% for mark in view.damage_marks %}
            <span class="mark" title="{{ mark.meaning or 'not in the printed legend' }}">
              <b>{{ mark.code }}</b> {{ mark.panel }}
            </span>
            {% endfor %}
          </div>
        </dd>
        {% endif %}

        {% if view.extraction %}
        {% if view.extraction.warnings_ja %}
        <dt>Warnings 注意事項欄</dt>
        <dd class="ja warn">{{ view.extraction.warnings_ja }}{% if view.extraction.warnings_en %}<span class="note translation">{{ view.extraction.warnings_en }}</span>{% endif %}</dd>
        {% endif %}

        {% if view.extraction.inspector_notes_ja %}
        <dt>Inspector's notes 検査員記入欄</dt>
        <dd class="ja">{{ view.extraction.inspector_notes_ja }}{% if view.extraction.inspector_notes_en %}<span class="note translation">{{ view.extraction.inspector_notes_en }}</span>{% endif %}</dd>
        {% endif %}

        {# Always rendered once a sheet is read, blank box included: it is the
           input the bid falls back to `private` on, and the card has to show
           what that assumption was made from. #}
        {% if view.history_note %}
        <dt>Vehicle history 車歴</dt>
        <dd class="ja {{ 'warn' if view.history_note.rental }}">
          {% if view.history_note.unset %}
          <span class="unset">unset — the sheet says neither</span>
          {% else %}
          {{ view.history_note.ja }}{% if view.history_note.en %}<span class="note translation">{{ view.history_note.en }}</span>{% endif %}
          {% endif %}
        </dd>
        {% endif %}

        {% if view.equipment %}
        <dt>Equipment</dt>
        <dd>
          <details>
            <summary>{{ view.equipment | length }} items</summary>
            <ul>{% for item in view.equipment %}<li class="ja">{{ item }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
          </details>
        </dd>
        {% endif %}
        {% endif %}{# view.extraction #}

        <dt>Cyprus</dt>
        <dd>
          {% if view.comp %}
          {{ view.comp.describe() }}
          {% else %}
          <span class="note">no comparable query (needs year + mileage)</span>
          {% endif %}
        </dd>

        <dt>Price</dt>
        <dd>
          start {{ lot.start_price_jpy | yen or '—' }}
          {% if jpy_per_eur and lot.start_price_jpy %}
          <span class="note">(≈ €{{ '{:,.0f}'.format(lot.start_price_jpy / jpy_per_eur) }}
            at {{ jpy_per_eur }} ¥/€)</span>
          {% endif %}
          {% if lot.end_price_jpy %}· sold {{ lot.end_price_jpy | yen }}{% endif %}
        </dd>

        {# max_bid − extra_costs = bid_reduced, or the reason there is no such
           number. Printed on every card in every group: a car that fails a
           requirement is still one whose price you may want to know, and the
           arithmetic does not depend on the verdict. Omitted only when the
           tables themselves are missing — that reason is report-wide and prints
           once in the header, rather than sixty times down the page. #}
        {% if view.quote %}
        <dt>Bid</dt>
        <dd class="money">
          {% for line in view.quote.lines() %}
          {% if loop.last %}
          <span class="{{ 'result' if view.quote.bid_reduced is not none else 'why' }}">{{ line }}</span>
          {% else %}
          <span>{{ line }}</span>
          {% endif %}
          {% endfor %}
        </dd>
        {% endif %}

        <dt>Links</dt>
        <dd class="note">
          {% if view.lot_url %}<a href="{{ view.lot_url }}">banzai24 lot page</a> · {% endif %}
          <code>{{ lot.lot_number }}</code>
          {% if view.extraction %}· read by {{ view.extraction.model_id }}
          {% if view.extraction.confidence is not none %}at confidence {{ '%.2f' % view.extraction.confidence }}{% endif %}
          {% endif %}
        </dd>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div>
</article>
{% endmacro %}

<header>
  <h1>{{ run_name }}</h1>
  <p class="meta">
    {{ views | length }} lot{{ '' if views | length == 1 else 's' }}
    {% if report.grouped %}
      {% for group in report.grouped %}· {{ group | length }} {{ group.label }} {% endfor %}
    {% else %}
    · {{ report.extracted }} with sheet data{% if report.unread %} ·
    {{ report.unread }} sheet{{ '' if report.unread == 1 else 's' }} not read yet{% endif %}
    {% endif %}
    {% if report.flagged %}· {{ report.flagged }} flagged{% endif %}
    · generated {{ generated_at }}
  </p>
  <ul class="notes">
    {% if report.missing %}
    <li>{{ report.missing | length }} lot(s) in this run are not in the database yet —
        run <code>normalize</code> to fill in what is known about them.</li>
    {% endif %}
    {% if report.definition is none %}
    <li>This run named no saved search, so nothing below is judged against
        requirements{% if report.search_reason %}: {{ report.search_reason }}{% endif %}.</li>
    {% elif report.search_reason %}
    <li>{{ report.search_reason }}.</li>
    {% endif %}
    {% if report.cyprus_reason %}
    <li>No Cyprus comparables: {{ report.cyprus_reason }}</li>
    {% endif %}
    {# The consequence clause is conditional because it is not always true: a
       mis-edited *alias* file is worth saying out loud, but the cards below
       still price — only the six houses it covers stop matching. #}
    {% if report.bid_reason %}
    <li>{{ report.bid_reason }}{% if not report.quoted %} — no bid price on any card below{% endif %}.</li>
    {% endif %}
  </ul>
</header>

<main>
{% if report.grouped %}
  {% for group in report.grouped %}
  <h2 class="group {{ group.key }}">{{ group.label }} <span class="n">· {{ group | length }}</span></h2>
  <p class="blurb">{{ group.blurb }}</p>
  {% for view in group.views %}{{ card(view) }}{% endfor %}
  {% endfor %}
{% else %}
  {% for view in views %}{{ card(view) }}{% else %}
  <p>No lots in this run.</p>
  {% endfor %}
{% endif %}
</main>

<footer>
  {% if report.definition %}
  <p>Judged against <code>{{ report.definition.name }}</code>:
     {{ report.definition.describe() }}</p>
  {% endif %}
  <p>Damage codes, as printed at the foot of every auction sheet:</p>
  <dl>
    {% for code, meaning in damage_codes.items() %}
    <dt><code>{{ code }}</code></dt><dd>{{ meaning }}</dd>
    {% endfor %}
  </dl>
  <p>A code carries a severity digit 1–4: <code>A1</code> is a light scratch,
     <code>U2</code> a more significant dent. A banned code is matched as a
     letter anywhere in the mark, so <code>X</code> catches <code>XX</code> and
     the severity digit is ignored. Cyprus figures are median <em>asking</em>
     prices from bazaraki.db, not sale prices.</p>
</footer>

</div>
</body>
</html>
